Titre$Dichotomous key to Xylariaceous genera

com$ tiré de http://pyrenomycetes.free.fr/xylariaceous  adapt gf fev 2012

1,5$Remarque importante
1,cs1 $ Xylariaceous fungi having multiperitheciate stromata (except Creosphaeria) that are not stalked nor with concentric fibrous rings $$s"groupe Hypoxylon"
1,cs2 $ Not (Xylariaceous fungi having multiperitheciate stromata (except Creosphaeria) that are not stalked nor with concentric fibrous rings )
5,0$ Un des auteurs a refusé la diffusion de ses clés (tirées du Web) au format cle : NE PAS DISTRIBUER !

cs1,0$ Key 1: genera formerly classified as Hypoxylon

TITRE$ Key 1: genera formerly classified as Hypoxylon
1,0 $ Stromata partially immersed, ascospores with    conspicuous poroid germ site $ Euepixylon
1,2 $ Stromata superficial, ascospores with elongated germ  slit, more rarely without apparent germ slit
2,0 $ Stromata crust-like, thick (>2mm), weakly attached to  the substrate $ Kretzschmaria
2,3 $ Stromata thinner, more widely attached to the substrate
3,4 $ Ascal apical ring discoid, broader than high
3,6 $ Ascal apical ring inverted hat-shaped, higher than broad
4,0 $ Stromata applanate or cupulate, carbonaceous, when  young with an outer dehiscing layer, without  KOH-extractable pigments $ Biscogniauxia
4,5 $ Stromata applanate, pulvinate or hemispherical, waxy,  usually coloured and yielding KOH-extractable pigments
5,0 $ Stromata uniperitheciate, coalescent in linear rows;  perithecia globose, large, > 1mm diam; anamorph  Libertella $ Creosphaeria
5,0 $ Stromata multiperitheciate; perithecia obovoid, tubular,  when globose <1mm diam; anamorph Nodulisporium-like $ Hypoxylon
6,0 $ Stromata erumpent from bark, perithecia large, > 1mm  diam $ Entoleuca
6,0 $ Stromata not erumpent, perithecia smaller $ Nemania


cs2,0$Key 2: other xylariaceous genera

1,2 $ On dung
1,5 $ Substrate different (de dung)
2,0 $ Stromata uniperitheciate, immersed $ Hypocopra
2,3 $ Stromata multiperitheciate, more or less stipitate
3,0 $ Asci lacking an apical ring $ Wawelia
3,4 $ Ascii with an apical ring
4,0 $ Stromata dicoid, flattened, on a short stipe $ Poronia
4,0 $ Stromata pulvinate to rounded, on a short to long filiform stipe $ Podosordaria
5,6 $ Stromata uniperitheciate
5,8 $ Stromata multiperitheciate
6,0 $ Each perithecium in a superficial subglobose stroma,  often associated with a subiculum $ Rosellinia
6,7 $ Each perithecium immersed in the substrate, under a  stroma reduced to a black clypeus
7,0 $ Ascospores one-celled $ Lopadostoma subg.  Anthostomopsis
7,0 $ Ascospores two-celled when young, cellular appendage  often present when mature $ Anthostomella s.l.
8,9 $ Stromata yielding pigments in 10% KOH
8,10 $ Pigments absent
9,0 $ Stromatal interior with concentric zones $ Daldinia
9,0 $ Stromatal interior hollow, filled with liquid when young $ Entonaema
10,0 $ Stromata stipitate constricted at base $ Xylaria
10,11 $ Stromata non-stipitate
11,0 $ Stromata effused in bark of Quercus, bipartite, very  inconspicuous; asci lacking apicalring $ Obolarina
11,0$ Stromata pustulate to effused, erumpent to superficial, frequently valsoid; on various hosts; ascal apical ring present Lopadostoma subg. $ Lopadostoma


Xylariaceous fungi: key to genera http://pyrenomycetes.free.fr/xylariaceous/keydir/dichotomickey.htm
